= Solution
{parent=ii}

For a Cartan subalgebra $\mathfrak h$, the root set consists of the nonzero linear functionals $\alpha\in\mathfrak h^*$ for which $\mathfrak g_\alpha=\{X:[H,X]=\alpha(H)X\}$ is nonzero. It is the <root system> of the Lie algebra.

Solved by gpt-5.6-sol high.

= iii
{parent=a}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=iii}

A <root string> through $\beta$ in the $\alpha$ direction is the uninterrupted sequence $\beta-p\alpha,\ldots,\beta+q\alpha$ of roots, with $p-q=\langle\beta,\alpha^\vee\rangle$.

Solved by gpt-5.6-sol high.

