The <classification of rank-two root systems> gives $A_1\times A_1$, $A_2$, $B_2$, and $G_2$. The first is reducible and corresponds to a semisimple but nonsimple algebra. Hence the complex simple rank-two algebras are $A_2$, $B_2=C_2$, and $G_2$, so $N=3$.

Solved by gpt-5.6-sol high.

= d
{parent=4}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=d}

This is the <G2 root system>, with $\alpha$ long and $\beta$ short. Its positive roots are
$$
\beta,\ \alpha,\ \alpha+\beta,\ \alpha+2\beta,\ \alpha+3\beta,\ 2\alpha+3\beta,
$$
and the full root set includes their negatives. Thus $\dim\mathfrak g=12+2=14$. Finally
$$
4\cos^2\theta=A_{12}A_{21}=3,
$$
and simple roots have obtuse angle, so $\theta=5\pi/6$.

Solved by gpt-5.6-sol high.

= e
{parent=4}
